sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2023-agential-09> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "In polyploid newts, whose cells are enlarged by extra genome copies, kidney tubules normally made by eight to ten communicating cells are instead formed by a single enormous cell wrapping around itself, so a different molecular mechanism (cytoskeletal bending rather than cell–cell communication) is deployed to reach the same anatomical outcome, an instance of downward causation in the service of a large-scale anatomical goal.";
    dc:type "empirical-generalization";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Polyploid newt kidney tubules are built by one giant cell instead of eight to ten";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Levin M, “Darwin's agential materials: evolutionary implications of multiscale competency in developmental biology”, Cellular and molecular life sciences : CMLS (2023), doi:10.1007/s00018-023-04790-z; section “Morphogenetic control as a collective intelligence”. Scope: Polyploid newt pronephric/kidney tubules"
}
